+# ICE3 Capture prototype
+
+Version 1.0.3-capture.1 / code 4 adds an isolated Capture launcher entry and a link from Snow3 Vision. The development branch combines current Bluetooth response fixes with the existing Jet Vision/App Actions work. Existing Recon connection owners and private Vision configuration are preserved.
+
+Capture uses the glasses Recom3Capture APK over a trusted private hotspot: an eight-digit pairing code bootstraps a random session token. The native controller receives JPEG camera preview / PNG display screenshots, saves local stills, and records incoming preview frames as silent H.264 MP4 on the phone. The viewer must stay visible; leaving it finalizes recording. Video is limited to two minutes / 128 MiB; starting another capture is refused once the folder exceeds 256 MiB, and a free-space check applies. An in-progress clip can grow beyond that start threshold. Sharing is restricted to that app-owned folder through FileProvider.
+
+The Jet display source requires a shell-UID helper explicitly started from an authorized PC. It does not require root, firmware/system APK replacement or network ADB. Restart the helper after a glasses reboot. See the Recom3Capture project for its scripts, device validation, known limitations and source protocol.
+
+A normal private hotspot is required: the prototype authenticates HTTP requests but does not implement TLS. No cloud upload or provider credential is added to Capture. Existing Vision provider functionality remains independent.
+
+The debug source set contains development instrumentation for real Wi-Fi source and phone encoder tests. Pairing configuration is provisioned as a temporary private file and removed by the verification script. These tests do not assert normal UI acceptance or background/locked recording support. Release builds do not package the instrumentation.
+
+Validation on the original Jet and Pixel 11: real camera photo and screenshot delivery, camera/display MP4 runs, complete-file decoding, 18 glasses HTTP host assertions and 123 existing ICE3 tests passed. Normal phone UI acceptance, Snow2 hardware, endurance and Android Auto coexistence remain pending.
\ No newline at end of file
