+# Jet Vision module
+
+Branch: `codex/jet-vision-file`. Adds an opt-in, separate **Snow3 Vision** launcher entry within the existing Snow3 APK. Jet camera JPEGs arrive through the original Recon Bluetooth FILE service, are verified in memory, analyzed with OpenAI `gpt-4.1-mini`, and answered over the existing OBJECT service. A separate provider adapter leaves Gemini configurable for later testing.
+
+The companion Jet project is `NEW_Recom_Apps/Recom3JetVision`. Its README and TEST_RESULTS document the full tested workflow, camera/transport evidence, measured latency and photo/WAV artifacts. Four actual OpenAI sessions succeeded, including while the Pixel was locked. The user confirmed clear Jet speech. This does not implement native Gemini/Android Auto invocation.
+
+## Configure privately
+
+Copy `vision.local.properties.example` to ignored `vision.local.properties` and enter your own key without sharing it in chat, source or build settings. Default provider/model: `openai` / `gpt-4.1-mini`. Enable Responses creation/write on a restricted key; the Images generation endpoint is not used. Do not add credentials to Gradle BuildConfig or assets.
+
+```powershell
+python tools/provision-vision.py --adb PATH_TO_ADB --serial PHONE_SERIAL
+```
+
+This provisions a debug APK's private `files/vision.properties` through ADB stdin/run-as; it never sends secrets as shell arguments or writes them to shared device storage. The file is excluded from backup. Open Snow3 Vision and reload its configuration after provisioning. The UI can disable analysis or delete the private configuration. A paid cloud request is sent only after a new Jet photograph passes integrity checks; there are no automatic retries or silent fallback providers.
+
+For Gemini later, set `vision.provider=gemini`, `gemini.model` and `gemini.api.key`. Its official generateContent adapter is present, but real Gemini validation has not been performed.
+
+## Session and compatibility
+
+Pair the Jet in system Bluetooth Settings, open Snow3 Vision, choose the paired Jet and Connect. The visible foreground session keeps network access with Android 17's lock screen active. Stop the session explicitly from its UI when done; this does not change battery/security settings or Open Headunit. The existing target SDK 28/compile SDK 28 toolchain remains unchanged; a future target-SDK upgrade will require reviewing modern foreground-service types/permissions.
+
+The root checkout's FILE handler previously ignored socket chunks. This branch assembles FILE frames on a separate bounded worker, retains original UUID/framing/GZIP, handles split headers/coalesced reads, resets for new FILE sockets and preserves non-Vision recipient delivery. Vision messages do not use the old shared-storage pointer path. That legacy path still has Android 17 public-storage limitations and is not a general scoped-storage migration.
+
+Cancellation can arrive on OBJECT before the FILE photograph; a bounded request/cancel cache prevents a late photo from starting inference. One JPEG is limited to 1 MiB and framed FILE messages to 2 MiB in this prototype. Cloud processing times out after 65 seconds. Keys/raw images are not logged; errors expose controlled summaries and exception class names only.
+
+Validation: `gradlew.bat :app:assembleDebug :app:testDebugUnitTest`; 119 tests, zero failures/errors, including original serial HTTP/maps/location tests and six new OpenAI/cancellation tests. Full physical legacy sync/maps regression remains outstanding. See the Jet application's TEST_RESULTS for precise session records and limitations. Existing build tooling and unrelated modules were preserved. No remote publication was performed.
+
+## Capture-launch follow-up
+
+The isolated `codex/jet-vision-app-actions` branch adds a local `recom3://vision/capture` entry and OPEN_APP_FEATURE shortcut declarations without changing FILE reception or cloud analysis. Real-device deep-link capture and the Jet Select fallback passed. Gemini voice invocation was not established; Android Auto voice invocation was not runtime-tested. Select remains the supported user control. See [VISION_APP_ACTIONS.md](VISION_APP_ACTIONS.md); the full Snow3 suite now passes 123 tests.
