+# Jet Vision launch and App Actions investigation
+
+Test date: 18 November 2026. Status: **Select remains the supported user control. The new phone deep link works; Google voice launch was not established.** The user ended further voice experiments for the night. No further voice engine has been implemented.
+
+## Implemented, separately from the photo pipeline
+
+Both repositories use local branch `codex/jet-vision-app-actions`, based on the previously validated `codex/jet-vision-file` code. Package/version remain `com.recom3.jetvision` 0.1.0 and `com.recom3.snow3` 1.0.2. Build toolchains, dependencies and permissions are unchanged.
+
+Snow3 adds an exported `VisionCaptureActivity` accepting exactly `recom3://vision/capture`, or an explicit ACTION_VIEW intent with inventory parameter `feature=jet_camera`. It binds the existing Recon connectivity service, requires its CONNECTED state, starts the existing opt-in foreground session, and sends one small `com.recom3.vision.CAPTURE` OBJECT envelope containing a random UUID. It does not reconnect or queue a capture for later. Invalid intents, recreation and repeat launches within ten seconds do not send a new command. The UI says command sent, not delivery confirmed.
+
+The Jet adds `JetCaptureReceiver` for this action, verifies bounded envelope shape, expected sender/action and UUID, and suppresses a bounded persisted history of duplicate UUIDs. It opens the existing camera activity. A small activity adapter waits up to eight seconds for the preview/resume state, then calls the same `capture()` method used by Select. Busy or paused activity handling prevents queued captures from firing later. Existing capture, FILE framing/transfer, JPEG verification, OpenAI request, result handling and speech remain unchanged. No Open Headunit or ReconOS source was modified.
+
+The old Recon broadcast transport does not authenticate third-party local applications cryptographically. Sender-field validation is a format/trust sanity check, not an authorization boundary. The capture deep link is intentionally public; this remains a private opt-in prototype, not a production camera security design.
+
+## Local invocation
+
+Connect the paired Jet using Snow3 Vision first, then:
+
+```powershell
+adb -s PIXEL_SERIAL shell am start -W -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d recom3://vision/capture com.recom3.snow3
+```
+
+This is local intent fulfillment testing, **not proof of Google voice recognition or App Actions registration**. [Google documents this ADB deep-link check separately from voice preview/deployment](https://developer.android.com/develop/devices/assistant/get-started).
+
+## Official App Actions declaration
+
+`res/xml/shortcuts.xml` declares `actions.intent.OPEN_APP_FEATURE`. A required `feature` parameter maps to the capture fulfillment activity; a parameter-free fallback opens the existing Vision screen without taking a photograph. Inline inventory shortcut `jet_camera` supplies English and Spanish feature names and a normal static launcher shortcut targeting the capture URI. `android.app.shortcuts` metadata is attached to Snow3 Vision's MAIN/LAUNCHER activity. Pixel ShortcutService registered `jet_camera` with the localized label `Foto con Jet`.
+
+[OPEN_APP_FEATURE requires feature inventory and lists supported locales, including es-ES](https://developer.android.com/reference/app-actions/built-in-intents/common/open-app-feature). This declaration follows the [documented shortcut/capability schema](https://developer.android.com/develop/devices/assistant/action-schema). It is not an arbitrary custom hotword or an instruction teaching Gemini a new application.
+
+The application's legacy application label is **ice3**; **Snow3 Vision** is an activity label. A production invocation name must match Google's registered app/preview naming. Renaming the local label alone does not register the capability.
+
+### Prerequisites not completed
+
+- Google documents Play Console access, matching development/device accounts, Play app availability and App Actions review/deployment. No Play upload, registration, terms acceptance or account change was performed.
+- The documented Assistant test tool requires Android Studio 4.0+ and access to the uploaded package with the same account. The inspected installed IDE build is AI-171.4443003 (3.0.1). No compatible preview was created. OPEN_APP_FEATURE inventory previews last six hours. [Official testing prerequisites](https://developer.android.com/develop/devices/assistant/test-tool).
+- Google's schema/build guide specifies AndroidX Core 1.6.0+. This legacy Support Library/AGP 3.0.1 application compiled and Android registered the static shortcut using existing attributes, without adding AndroidX. That empirical packaging success does not establish compliance with the full documented App Actions setup. A reviewed AndroidX/build migration would be separate work; none was attempted.
+- General Gemini AppFunctions/Android MCP is a different integration. Its official workflow requires developer-preview access, a linked Play app, implemented AppFunctions, account permissions and a new app bundle. No such integration is present. [Google's prerequisites](https://developer.android.com/ai/appfunctions/create-manage-connected-apps).
+
+## Physical results
+
+Devices: original Recon Jet, Android 4.1.2/API 16; Pixel 11, Android 17. Both USB-authorized; existing bonded Recon Bluetooth channels reused. No security settings changed.
+
+| Scenario | Observed result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Deep link while disconnected | Explicit `notConnected`; no photograph queued. Existing Snow3 Connect button re-established channels after APK update. |
+| Deep link while connected | **Passed end to end.** Command token `2fcb5974-f099-4a8e-a7e7-eacd58258541` received on Jet; capture request `1815516194`; 130,831-byte 1280 x 960 JPEG; matching SHA-256 `020226adae3e67a6bb765f06f4603efc69dbc0fd869db424e12219e91201fb9f`. One OpenAI attempt, HTTP 200; Jet result in 32,866 ms; speech completion logged. |
+| Select fallback after launch additions | **Passed end to end.** Request `1815729766`; 131,932-byte JPEG, SHA-256 `1514ad12fd7733bd5a436a415419b94173d5291c12147f117836009a5805828a`; result in 20,852 ms and speech completion. |
+| Unknown query (`capture?count=2`) | Handler launched but rejected the intent; routing tests also cover altered scheme/host/path/query/fragment and parameter overrides. No capture is intended for these routes. |
+| Phone voice attempt | **Not established.** First “try again” replies were identified as Voice Match training, not an App Actions failure. After leaving training, user reported Gemini did not know Snow3 Vision/Jet and could not open apps in that interaction. No separately correlated voice-originated capture was established. An earlier user report of capture was not counted because it overlapped the ADB test. |
+| Alternate name `ice3` | Suggested after confirming the legacy label. No verified successful feature invocation recorded. |
+| Gemini through Android Auto | **Not runtime-tested in this follow-up.** Testing paused during voice setup and then ended at user request. Separate documentation restrictions below; do not misreport as an observed car failure. |
+
+The network/API and Bluetooth timing varied; these are two individual checks, not latency benchmarks. Existing prior evidence/photo/WAV and validation report remain available and unchanged.
+
+## Android Auto restrictions
+
+Google's current [App Actions for Cars guide](https://developer.android.com/develop/devices/assistant/cars) limits this integration to Car App Library POI apps and the parking/charging BIIs. It does not list OPEN_APP_FEATURE or general camera control. Snow3 has no Car App Library service and no eligible parking/charging functionality. No navigation impersonation, car-category metadata or undocumented Google API was added.
+
+Working Maps voice navigation uses a supported car integration; it does not mean arbitrary app deep links can be invoked by Gemini in Android Auto. The phone test and car restrictions are distinct. Simultaneous Open Headunit projection plus this separate camera activity was not tested. Receiving the capture command brings Jet Vision to the foreground, which can naturally affect another activity's lifecycle.
+
+## Build, tests and fallbacks
+
+- Both debug APK builds passed with the unchanged Gradle 4.1 / AGP 3.0.1 / JDK 8 toolchains.
+- Snow3: **123 tests, zero failures**, including four new intent-routing tests and the existing 119 tests.
+- Jet: **17 protocol checks passed**. Lint: zero errors, four warnings (intentional old target, exported legacy OBJECT receiver, missing dedicated icon, app indexing). No new permissions or native libraries.
+- Original pre-voice APKs are retained under `artifacts/app-actions/fallback/`; the original root APK copies were not overwritten.
+- Updated APKs and filtered module logs are under `artifacts/app-actions/`; artifacts and credentials remain Git-ignored. Installation used update-in-place, preserving private cloud configuration. No keys are packaged in the Vision module.
+- No push, PR, Play upload, firmware modification, rooting, uninstall or change to Open Headunit was performed.
+
+## Recommended next step
+
+Use Select as the primary control now. The new capture URI is available for local integrations but is not advertised as working Gemini voice control. No additional action is needed from the user tonight.
+
+For a later glasses-side “take photo” feature, first prototype an explicitly enabled, small-vocabulary offline recognizer against the Jet microphone and API-16/ARMv7 hardware, then validate accuracy, battery, camera/audio coexistence and false activation handling. The inspected Jet package registry did not advertise an Android speech RecognitionService or RECOGNIZE_SPEECH handler. A new recognizer is therefore required; changing the phrase alone cannot add it. [Android provides availability checks and warns that SpeechRecognizer is not intended for continuous recognition](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/speech/SpeechRecognizer). No custom voice engine or continuous microphone capture was implemented during this task.
